<title>JORDAN: Jordanian bank assets rise slightly in March.</title>
<headline>Jordanian bank assets rise slightly in March.</headline>
<dateline>AMMAN 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total assets of Jordanian banks rose slightly in March to 8.880 billion dinars ($12.52 billion) from 8.876 billion dinars in February, the Central Bank statistical bulletin said.</p>
<p>Total deposits with licenced banks slipped to 6.043 billion dinars from 6.051 billion dinars and foreign currency deposits were also slightly down at 2.27 billion dinars.</p>
<p>(All figures in million of dinars)</p>
<p>			  Mar 1997  Feb 1997   Mar 1996  1996   1995</p>
<p>    Total Assets    8,880     8,876	8,437     8,858  8,430</p>
<p>    Total deposits  6,043     6,051	5,845     5,989  5,788</p>
<p>Foreign currency deposits:</p>
<p>			  2,273     2,310	2,256     2,334  2,255</p>
<p>NOTE -- The figures cover Jordan's 19 licensed banks including six investment banks and five subsidiaries of foreign banks operating under similar Central Bank rules.</p>
<p>$1=0.709 dinar</p>
<p>Amman newsroom, 962 6 623 776</p>
